Washington D.C. — Today, U.S. Rep. Terri Sewell (AL-07) announced that she secured $9,571,000 in direct funding for 14 local projects in Alabama's 7th Congressional District. Funding for these projects was passed by Congress and signed into law as a part of the Fiscal Year 2026 appropriations process.

Watch Rep. Sewell's social media video here.

"I’m so proud to have secured $9.5 million for 14 community-driven projects that will make our district safer, stronger, and more prosperous," said Rep. Sewell. "These investments reflect the priorities I hear from families, local leaders, and small businesses every day—safer streets, better infrastructure, and more opportunity. I will keep fighting to bring resources back to our community and to ensure that every federal dollar works for the people I represent.”

